{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-009", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China's VSF surge of 1.74% puts Asia's fibre cost balance at risk", "content": "Asian VSF markets closed the week ended September 5, 2026, with regional divergence as Chinese 1.5D×38mm domestic VSF rose 1.74 per cent.\nIndian 1.4D and 1.5D×38mm grades were unchanged at ₹196/kg and ₹193/kg; Pakistan’s 1.5D held at PKR 636/kg.\nChina’s rise narrowed intra-Asia price differentials and changed the relative attractiveness of regional sourcing routes for procurement teams.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-s-vsf-surge-of-1-74-puts-asia-s-fibre-cost-balance-at-risk-313294-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-010", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "sustainable_textile", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Pakistan's 3.95% organic cotton jump gives India a cost edge", "content": "Pakistan’s KCA spot rate for Above-26 mm organic cotton rose 3.95 per cent on September 1 to 704.7696 PKR/kg, then held through Friday.\nIndia’s Shankar-6 organic cotton stayed at ₹226/kg, while pre-consumer recycled cotton remained at ₹151/kg.\nThe move created a clear price divergence between two major Asian cotton markets despite a sharp late-week reversal in global cotton prices.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/pakistan-s-3-95-organic-cotton-jump-gives-india-a-cost-edge-313289-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-011", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "JCRA raises India’s sovereign credit rating to A-", "content": "JCRA has raised India’s sovereign rating to A- from BBB+, putting the country back in A-grade territory after its last A-level rating in 1988.\nThe move follows 2025 upgrades by Morningstar DBRS, R&I and S&P, widening overseas recognition of stronger fundamentals.\nFor exporters, manufacturers and lenders, higher sovereign credit standing can influence borrowing costs and investor appetite.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/jcra-raises-india-s-sovereign-credit-rating-to-a--313282-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-012", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam sets clearer licensing rules for foreign-invested e-commerce", "content": "Vietnam has issued Decree No. 342/2026/ND-CP, clarifying licensing and market access rules for foreign-invested trading and e-commerce businesses. \nThe decree covers intermediary and integrated e-commerce platforms and social networks engaged in e-commerce. \nProvincial People’s Committees will handle licensing, while investors must meet treaty, tax, security and sector-specific requirements.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-sets-clearer-licensing-rules-for-foreign-invested-e-commerce-313283-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-013", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India cotton yarn remains stable amid new arrival season", "content": "Cotton yarn prices stayed unchanged in Ludhiana and Delhi as north India demand cooled and buyers turned cautious before the cotton marketing season. \nPanipat recycled yarn saw average demand; cotton comber and recycled polyester fibre steadied after last week’s ₹3-5 per kg rise. \nNew cotton arrivals in Haryana and Rajasthan pushed prices down by ₹50-60 per maund, with Punjab arrivals negligible. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-cotton-yarn-remains-stable-amid-new-arrival-season-313279-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-014", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Pakistan's BCI cotton jump 4.21% puts India's yarn edge in focus", "content": "Asia’s domestic cotton benchmarks moved in sharply different directions from August 31 to September 4, 2026, showing distinct price-formation mechanisms.\nPakistan’s BCI KCA Spot rose 4.21 per cent after a KCA revision, while China’s BCI 3128B fell 1.25 per cent as Xinjiang’s new crop pressured prices.\nIndia’s BCI Shankar-6 stayed unchanged at ₹199.00/kg, reflecting MSP support.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/pakistan-s-bci-cotton-jump-4-21-puts-india-s-yarn-edge-in-focus-313278-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-015", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["order_visibility", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US apparel imports are weak; so why did bookings jump 79%?", "content": "US HS61–62 apparel imports fell 7.77 per cent to $36.90 billion in H1 2026, but the contraction narrowed from 11.82 per cent in Q1 to 3.28 per cent in Q2.\nClothing and accessories-store sales rose 5.9 per cent to $151.09 billion; June's inventory-to-sales ratio fell to 2.14.\nUS-bound HS61–62 ocean bookings reached 21,434 TEU in June, up 79 per cent, led by Vietnam and Cambodia.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-apparel-imports-are-weak-so-why-did-bookings-jump-79--313285-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-07-016", "date": "2026-09-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["improve", "concerns", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s RMG sector bets on technology for a productivity edge", "content": "Bangladesh apparel exporters are adopting digital monitoring, data-driven production and AI tools to raise productivity, reduce downtime and improve quality.\nSome factories report gains of up to 25 per cent versus manual monitoring, though results vary by technology, conditions and measurement.\nThe shift also raises concerns over worker pressure, privacy and fair sharing of productivity gains.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-rmg-sector-bets-on-technology-for-a-productivity-edge-313242-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
